.TH PEPAD 1 "24 July 2026" "PepAD 1.42" "PepAD User Manual"
.
.SH NAME
PepAD \- Peptide Assembly Design Algorithm
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B PepAD
.br
.B PepAD
.BR \-h
.br
.B PepAD
.BR \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PepAD
performs sequence design for peptide assemblies using Monte Carlo
sequence moves and molecular energy calculations.
For a normal design run, a file named
.I input.txt
must be present in the directory where PepAD is started.
All design parameters are read from this file and are not accepted as
command-line options.
.
.PP
Every parameter in
.I input.txt
must use the following format:
.
.RS
.nf
PARAMETER = value
.fi
.RE
.
.PP
The equal sign is required.
Parameter order does not matter.
Comments may begin with
.B #
or
.BR ! .
Each input parameter may appear only once.
Only
.B PDBFILE
and
.B N_STEPS
are required.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the PepAD help information and stop.
.
.PP
Any other command-line option is rejected.
All design parameters must be placed in
.IR input.txt .
.
.SH REQUIRED INPUT PARAMETERS
.TP
.B PDBFILE
String.
Filename of the initial PDB structure.
.TP
.B N_STEPS
Integer.
Number of Monte Carlo steps.
.
.SH INITIAL STRUCTURE PARAMETERS
.B PepAD
automatically determines the number of amino acids, number of chains,
energy-group assignment, and beta-sheet assignment from the PDB file.
If the user supplies these parameters in
.IR input.txt ,
the user-supplied assignments override the automatically determined
assignments.
.
.TP
.B N_AA
Integer.
Optional user-defined number of amino acids per peptide chain.
ACE, NME, and NHE cap residues are excluded from this number.
.TP
.B N_CHAINS
Integer.
Optional user-defined total number of peptide chains.
.B N_AA
and
.B N_CHAINS
must either both be supplied or both be omitted.
.TP
.BR GROUP_1 ", " GROUP_2
Integer lists.
Optional user-defined chain IDs belonging to each energy-calculation
group.
.TP
.BR SHEET_1 ", " SHEET_2 ", ..."
Integer lists.
Optional user-defined chain IDs belonging to each beta-sheet.
.TP
.B RESTART
Integer.
Use 0 for a fresh run or 1 for a restart.
The default is 0.
.
.PP
When no user assignments are supplied, PepAD determines
.BR N_AA ,
.BR N_CHAINS ,
the energy groups, and the beta-sheets from the PDB structure.
Energy groups and beta-sheets are determined using DSSP-based
analysis.
.
.SH MONTE CARLO AND ENERGY PARAMETERS
.TP
.B RANSEED
Integer.
Random-number seed.
If this parameter is omitted, PepAD generates a seed from the current
system clock time.
If it is supplied, PepAD uses the user-provided seed.
.TP
.B KBT_SEQ
Real.
Sequence kBT used when
.BR ANNEAL_STAGES " = 0."
The default is 1.0.
.TP
.B KBT_SEQ_HIGH
Real.
Initial sequence kBT when
.B ANNEAL_STAGES
is greater than 0.
The default is 2.0.
.TP
.B KBT_SEQ_LOW
Real.
Final sequence kBT when
.B ANNEAL_STAGES
is greater than 0.
The default is 0.5.
.TP
.B KBT_SHEETMOVE
Real.
Sheet-move kBT used when
.BR ANNEAL_STAGES " = 0."
The default is 0.6.
.TP
.B KBT_SHEETMOVE_HIGH
Real.
Initial sheet-move kBT when
.B ANNEAL_STAGES
is greater than 0.
The default is 1.2.
.TP
.B KBT_SHEETMOVE_LOW
Real.
Final sheet-move kBT when
.B ANNEAL_STAGES
is greater than 0.
The default is 0.3.
.TP
.B RMSD_MAX
Real.
Maximum RMSD in angstroms.
The default is 3.0.
.TP
.B PAGG_WEIGHT
Real.
Aggregation-propensity weight.
The default is 2.0.
.TP
.B SHEETMOVE
Integer.
Use 0 to disable sheet-position perturbation moves or 1 to enable them.
The default is 1.
.TP
.B ANNEAL_STAGES
Integer.
Use 0 for no annealing or a positive integer for the number of
annealing stages.
The default is 0.
.TP
.B ESURF_MODE
Integer.
Use 0 to disable non-polar solvation energy, 1 for the direct full
ARVO reference calculation, or 2 for the cached/incremental ARVO
calculation.
The default is 0.
.TP
.B STEPS_BEFORE_SHEETMOVE
Integer.
Number of initial waiting steps before a sheet move.
The default is 500.
.TP
.B STEPS_BETWEEN_SHEETMOVE
Integer.
Number of sequence steps between sheet-move opportunities.
The default is 200.
.
.SH COMPOSITION PARAMETERS
.TP
.B N_HYDROPHOBIC_MIN
Integer.
Minimum number of hydrophobic amino acids.
.TP
.B N_HYDROPHOBIC_MAX
Integer.
Maximum number of hydrophobic amino acids.
.TP
.B N_POLAR_MIN
Integer.
Minimum number of polar amino acids.
.TP
.B N_POLAR_MAX
Integer.
Maximum number of polar amino acids.
.TP
.B N_CHARGED_MIN
Integer.
Minimum number of charged amino acids.
.TP
.B N_CHARGED_MAX
Integer.
Maximum number of charged amino acids.
.TP
.B N_OTHER_MIN
Integer.
Minimum number of other-category amino acids.
.TP
.B N_OTHER_MAX
Integer.
Maximum number of other-category amino acids.
.
.PP
If all category flags are omitted, PepAD uses the composition of the
initial PDB structure.
In custom composition mode, every category requires a minimum, a
maximum, or both.
An omitted minimum becomes 0, and an omitted maximum becomes
.BR N_AA .
Equal minimum and maximum values specify a fixed category count.
.
.PP
Composition totals exclude ACE, NME, and NHE cap residues.
Single-site and grouped-site amino acids are included in the
composition totals.
Fixed single-site amino acids contribute to the required
amino-acid and category minimums.
.
.SH COMPOSITIONAL CONSTRAINTS
.TP
.B N_<AA>_MIN
Integer.
Minimum count of the specified amino acid.
.TP
.B N_<AA>_MAX
Integer.
Maximum count of the specified amino acid.
.
.PP
Supported amino-acid identifiers are:
.
.RS
.nf
GLY ALA VAL LEU ILE MET PHE TYR TRP SER
ASN GLN THR HIE ARG LYS GLU ASP CYS PRO
.fi
.RE
.
.PP
Users may provide only a minimum, only a maximum, or both.
Equal minimum and maximum values impose an exact amino-acid count.
An amino acid without either flag is unrestricted.
Each
.B N_<AA>_MIN
or
.B N_<AA>_MAX
flag may appear only once.
Specific-amino-acid minimums cannot exceed the corresponding category
maximum.
.
.SH POSITIONAL CONSTRAINTS
ACE, NME, and NHE cap positions are handled automatically.
User-supplied site numbers refer only to amino acids; cap positions
are skipped.
For example, amino-acid position 3 is chain residue position 4 when
chain residue position 1 is an ACE cap.
.
.TP
.B SINGLE_SITE_CONSTRAINTS
Sites that remain unchanged during the design run.
A site number without an amino-acid name retains the amino acid from
the initial structure.
For example:
.
.RS
.nf
SINGLE_SITE_CONSTRAINTS = 3 5
.fi
.RE
.
.IP
A
.B site:AA
entry changes the site to the specified amino acid and then keeps it
unchanged.
For example:
.
.RS
.nf
SINGLE_SITE_CONSTRAINTS = 3:CYS 12:LEU
.fi
.RE
.
.IP
Separate entries with spaces and do not place spaces around the colon.
.
.TP
.B GROUPED_SITE_AA_POOL
Allowed amino-acid copies for the grouped sites.
For example:
.
.RS
.nf
GROUPED_SITE_AA_POOL = ASN SER ALA ALA
.fi
.RE
.
.IP
Repeated amino acids are allowed.
Each remaining pool copy has an equal selection probability, so
repeated entries increase that amino acid's selection probability.
The number of pool entries must be at least the number of grouped-site
constraints.
.
.TP
.B GROUPED_SITE_CONSTRAINTS
Amino-acid sites that select from the available grouped-site pool
copies.
For example:
.
.RS
.nf
GROUPED_SITE_CONSTRAINTS = 4 6 10 12
.fi
.RE
.
.PP
PepAD checks grouped-pool category minimums and maximums against the
overall composition limits.
Caps and positional-constraint sites are excluded from ordinary Monte
Carlo site selection.
.
.SH EXAMPLE INPUT
.nf
# Required parameters
PDBFILE = assembly.pdb
N_STEPS = 10000

# Optional structure information
N_AA = 7
N_CHAINS = 8

# Optional fixed composition
N_HYDROPHOBIC_MIN = 5
N_HYDROPHOBIC_MAX = 5
N_POLAR_MIN = 0
N_POLAR_MAX = 0
N_CHARGED_MIN = 2
N_CHARGED_MAX = 2
N_OTHER_MIN = 0
N_OTHER_MAX = 0
.fi
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I input.txt
Required parameter file for a normal PepAD design run.
It must be present in the directory where PepAD is started.
.TP
.I pdbfiles/
Directory containing generated PDB structures and SCMF diagnostic
structures.
.
.SH AUTHORS
Haoyu Wang, Sudeep Sarma, and Carol K. Hall.
.
.SH VERSION
PepAD version 1.42.
